[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Eurobot System Requirements

[GRAMMAR]
IMPORT_FROM_FILE: @eurobot

[TEXT]
STATEMENT: >>>
System (black box) requirements. Each requirement declares a ``COVERS``
relation to every ``RULE`` it addresses. ``RULE-7.1`` is deliberately left
uncovered, so the Traceability Matrix shows what an unaddressed rule looks
like.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-1
TITLE: Footprint at start
STATEMENT: >>>
The robot shall fit, at the start of the match, inside a perimeter of
1200 mm measured around its footprint.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-4.1
  ROLE: COVERS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-2
TITLE: Height without beacon support
STATEMENT: >>>
The robot shall measure at most 350 mm from the table surface to its
highest point, with the beacon support removed.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-4.2
  ROLE: COVERS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-3
TITLE: Emergency stop cuts actuator power
STATEMENT: >>>
Pressing the emergency stop button shall remove power from every motor
and every actuator within 100 ms, and the robot shall stay unpowered
until the button is released.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-5.1
  ROLE: COVERS

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: REQ-4
TITLE: Autonomous match cycle
STATEMENT: >>>
After the starter is pulled, the robot shall run its match strategy
without any operator input and shall stop all motion 100 seconds later.
<<<
RELATIONS:
- TYPE: Parent
  VALUE: RULE-6.1
  ROLE: COVERS
